    {
      "name": "graduate",
      "docs": [
        "Graduates a completed curve into a deep-amm (DeepSwap CPMM) pool, non-custodially:",
        "the pool is created via CPI with `lp_sol` (as WSOL) and `lp_tokens` from",
        "`math::graduation_allocation`, every LP token received is burned (permanent",
        "lock), and reserve tokens not needed for the pool are burned. The pool is created",
        "through deep-amm `initialize_with_permission`, so it charges the AmmConfig's",
        "creator fee, records the TOKEN's creator as its `pool_creator` (who can collect",
        "their share) and takes that fee in SOL on both trade directions. The migration",
        "authority only triggers it and never holds funds. Pool creation costs",
        "(deep-amm create-pool fee + rent) are paid out of the migration fee; the rest",
        "goes to the treasury. If the migration fee does not cover the costs, anyone can",
        "top up the `pool_creator` PDA with SOL and retry (that PDA is shared by every",
        "graduation, and each one sweeps what is left of it to the Treasury, so top up in",
        "the same transaction or right before the retry). Idempotent: a second call",
        "fails with `AlreadyGraduated`."
      ],
      "discriminator": [45, 235, 225, 181, 17, 218, 64, 130],
      "accounts": [
        {
          "name": "migration_authority",
          "docs": [
            "Must be the configured migration authority (expected: a multisig). Triggers",
            "graduation and fronts the two temporary ATAs' rent (refunded); never holds funds."
          ],
          "writable": true,
